  "result": "That's a big question!\n\nIf I could pick just one thing, it would be to give everyone a little more *felt* empathy for each other \u2014 like the ability to really feel, for just a moment, what it's like to walk in someone else's shoes.\n\nNot to erase disagreement \u2014 differences are what make the world interesting \u2014 but so much conflict, loneliness, and cruelty comes from forgetting that the other person is just as real, complicated, and trying their best as we are.\n\nI think if that sense of shared humanity was our default, a lot of the other big problems \u2014 poverty, polarization, climate inaction, wars \u2014 would become a lot easier to solve together. We'd still argue about *how* to fix things, but we'd actually want to fix them *for each other*.\n\nWhat about you? If you had one wish for the world, what would you pick?",
